  "worked_solution": "The net of our prism is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/7b84a48933abb96f605476c6d703406227b0fe5301b1457a447cdbb3f58f0937.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nEach side face (apart from the square faces) of our solid is a rectangle, where the base is $7\\,\\text{ft}$ and the height is $4\\,\\text{ft}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=7\\times 4=28\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, the total area of the side surfaces consists of $4$ rectangular faces. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area of the sides} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle}) \\\\  & =4\\times 28 \\\\  & =112\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the cost to paint the surface is $$6.50$ per square foot, the total amount that Chloe will have to pay is\n\n$$\n112\\times 6.50=$728.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
